    "outcome": {
      "A": "Final x Decided(Yes) at finalize; adapter execute at 1791522804 (about 31 h after the judgment window closed) -> acceptFulfillment accepted and paid: the kernel bounds acceptFulfillment by settleBy only and settleBy = 0; Enacted; submission 9/1 Accepted",
      "A2": "Final x NoDecision (round 2 closed without ballots, REQUIRE_FRESH_DECISION); claimUnjudged(10, 1) paid the worker by the kernel default; submission 10/1 Accepted"
    },
    "record": "deployments/sepolia-first-attempt.json (written by CloseFirstAttempt) and deployments/sepolia-first-attempt-input.json (its input)",
    "lesson": "the adapter's own deadline (judgment window minus margin, decision #36) is the conservative bound it uses at open; whether a late acceptance is still legal is the kernel's call at execute, recorded as Enacted or Failed. Here the kernel accepted. A missed Finalize is therefore a bookkeeping gap, not a loss of funds in either direction, and the kernel default covers the NoDecision case."
  },
